-- title:
--   DVR stalks persist under base change to a DVR extension
-- statement:
--   Let $A_0$ be a discrete valuation ring which is a domain, with a chosen element $\varpi_0$ generating its maximal ideal, and let $A_1$ be a discrete valuation ring which is a domain, with a chosen element $\varpi_1$ generating its maximal ideal. Let $\iota_1'\colon A_0\to A_1$ be an injective local ring homomorphism such that the composite of $\iota_1'$ with the residue map $A_1\to A_1/\mathfrak m_{A_1}$ is surjective, i.e. $A_0$ already surjects onto the residue field of $A_1$. Let $X_0$ be an integral scheme over $\operatorname{Spec} A_0$ via a morphism $\mathrm{toBase}_0$ which is flat and locally of finite presentation. Let $X_1$ be a scheme with morphisms $f_1\colon X_1\to\operatorname{Spec} A_1$ and $g_1\colon X_1\to X_0$ forming a pullback square for $\mathrm{toBase}_0$ and $\operatorname{Spec}(\iota_1')$. Let $\eta_1\in X_1$ be a point whose image under $f_1$ is the closed point of $\operatorname{Spec} A_1$, and suppose the stalk $\mathcal O_{X_0,g_1(\eta_1)}$ is a discrete valuation ring whose maximal ideal is generated by the image of $\varpi_0$ under the structure map $A_0\to\Gamma(X_0,\mathcal O_{X_0})\to\mathcal O_{X_0,g_1(\eta_1)}$. The conclusion asserts that $\mathcal O_{X_1,\eta_1}$ is a domain, that it is a discrete valuation ring, and that its maximal ideal is generated by the image of $\varpi_1$ under $A_1\to\Gamma(X_1,\mathcal O_{X_1})\to\mathcal O_{X_1,\eta_1}$.
--
--   This is the step which propagates the discrete-valuation-ring property of a stalk, together with the fact that a uniformiser of the base generates the maximal ideal of that stalk, along a base change of the base discrete valuation ring that does not enlarge the residue field. It is used in the construction of a valuation subring as the range of a stalk map at a point in the smooth locus, where the valuation ring of the limit is exhausted by such stalks over the finite levels; the proof rests on the description of the stalk of a pullback as a localisation of a tensor product, [`AlgebraicGeometry.exists_ringEquiv_stalk_pullback_localization_tensorProduct_stalk_of_germ_snd`](thm.html#AlgebraicGeometry.exists_ringEquiv_stalk_pullback_localization_tensorProduct_stalk_of_germ_snd).
